{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","text":"Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/d